PHASE 3 — direct reproduction with prod GUC pattern
---------------------------------------------------

Reproduction query (matches the asyncpg pool setup callback behaviour
in smartbi.tenant_ctx.set_pg_connection_tenant):

  SET ROLE smartbi_user;
  SELECT set_config('app.factory_id', '__internal__', false);
  INSERT INTO smart_bi_llm_usage
    (provider, model, caller, input_tokens, output_tokens, total_tokens, factory_id)
    VALUES ('test', 'test', 'repro-590', 0, 0, 0, NULL);

Result:
  SET
   set_config
  --------------
   __internal__
  (1 row)

  ERROR: new row violates row-level security policy for table
         "smart_bi_llm_usage"

This is the exact failure path of common.llm_metrics._flush_loop.


PHASE 4 — control: GUC unset (PR #576's tested path)
----------------------------------------------------

  SET ROLE smartbi_user;
  -- no set_config — GUC defaults to NULL
  INSERT INTO smart_bi_llm_usage (provider, model, caller, factory_id, ...)
    VALUES (..., NULL) RETURNING id;

Result:
   id
  ------
   6430
  (1 row)
  INSERT 0 1

So PR #576's policy correctly allows GUC-unset + NULL factory_id. But
the prod flush loop never has GUC unset — the pool setup callback always
writes the '__internal__' sentinel. That's the test gap PR #576 missed.


PHASE 5 — apply fix (V20260515_01)
----------------------------------

Migration: DROP + CREATE tenant_insert policy, adding '__internal__'
to both the NULL-factory_id and the tenant-factory_id branches.

Result:
  DROP POLICY
  CREATE POLICY


